      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6a365281c7883eb12336cef940bddf4303065a16bb82f4cd20ea53b3549047f8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source places approximation freedom on either side of the same overlap: it can keep the Riemann–Siegel evolution fixed and reweight the reference state to obtain the smoother Berry–Keating expression with its first correction, or it can keep the overlap objective while allowing effective dynamics with inaccurate termwise phases because periodicity, amplitude decay, and cross-term compensation preserve the aggregate output.",
